<title>JAPAN: Japan may use satellite to check grain output.</title>
<headline>Japan may use satellite to check grain output.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Agriculture Ministry is considering using a satellite to monitor grain output in the Asia region, a ministry official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The ministry will launch three-year feasibility study next year, spending 13 million yen for fiscal 1996/97, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;We'll start analysing satellite pictures of Indonesian farm land next year as a first step. Our final goal is to establish a system to gather information about Asian grain output,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Japan currently depends heavily on the United States Department of Agriculture for such information.</p>
</text>
